# Completed local bodies retain their actual layout through A and admission
# to B. C.y and D.y have different physical source slots; the held value,
# not its factory prototype or its narrowed contract A, chooses the map.
A: (int: x 1)
B: (int: y 2)
fn: makeC () A
    C: (int: x 11; int: y 22; int: pad 33)
    return: @C
fn: makeD () A
    D: (int: x 11; int: pad 55; int: y 44)
    return: @D
fn: readB (B: value) int
    return: value\y
@: A p makeC()
int: first readB(p)
p: makeD()
int: second readB(p)
int: ok 0
if: first = 22 && second = 44
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
